# Everything here is LF, in the object store AND in every working tree.
#
# This repo is developed on Windows with core.autocrlf=true, so without this
# rule every file is checked out with CRLF while the blobs themselves stay LF.
# Measured on this repo: 0 of 483 committed text blobs contain CRLF, while 273
# of their working-tree copies do.
#
# The cost is that `prettier --check` becomes unreadable. Of the 251 files it
# currently flags across src/ and tests/, 174 are flagged for the line ending
# alone - prettier's `endOfLine` defaults to "lf" - and only 67 have anything
# actually wrong with them. A check that is three-quarters noise is a check
# nobody reads, which is how those 67 went unnoticed.
#
# Because the blobs are already LF this only pins the working tree to match what
# is committed; no history is rewritten and no file content changes. It does not
# fix the 67; it just makes them visible.
#
# Git attributes are per-repository and do not follow into or out of a
# submodule, which is why the monorepo root, administrative-document and
# crm-frontend each carry their own copy rather than inheriting one.
* text=auto eol=lf

# The one binary asset in the tree. `text=auto` would detect it, but saying so
# costs nothing and removes the guess.
*.png binary
